    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 10th looking to capitalize on high-upside matchups, led by **Trea Turner** (78.26), who is our clear top play. Facing Sugano, **Trea Turner** benefits from an elite SP skill matchup (+18%) and an optimal leadoff spot, making him the cornerstone of our pursuit of stolen bases and runs. **Kyle Schwarber** (74.74) pairs beautifully with **Trea Turner** in the top-of-the-order, bolstered by an elite 0.395 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Sugano. While **Yordan Alvarez** (72.28) faces a challenging lefty in Abbott, his elite 0.428 xwOBA makes him an auto-start despite the platoon disadvantage. Notably, **Dillon Dingler** (60.86) and **Junior Caminero** (63.50) provide strong mid-tier production, with **Dillon Dingler** specifically benefiting from a +14% dynamic platoon boost against Noah Cameron.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Chase Meidroth** (37.95) on the bench. Despite a solid base projection, his score plummeted due to the daunting task of facing Gilbert, an elite arm, pushing him well below our 40-point efficiency floor. We are exercising caution with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (52.12); while his speed is vital to our stolen base strategy, his matchup against deGrom is a high-risk scenario. The -19% SP skill penalty highlights the difficulty of facing an elite ace, and we are monitoring his performance closely to see if he can overcome the raw matchup data. Elsewhere, we continue to track the health of **Christian Yelich**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and the MiLB status of **Zac Veen**, leaving our active depth, including **Josh Smith**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena**, on standby should any last-minute lineup adjustments arise for **Colt Keith** or **Dillon Dingler**.",
